-- the medium is a chiral environment exactly when some chiral constituent is present in excess over its
-- mirror image. Pirkle's 1966 paper is titled for this fact: the nonequivalence of physical properties of
-- enantiomers in optically active solvents (J. Am. Chem. Soc. 88:1837), and the agent that carries his
-- name, 1-(9-anthryl)-2,2,2-trifluoroethanol, works only as a single enantiomer.
mixture-chiral : Mixture → Bool
mixture-chiral m = case m of
  nil → false
  cons c r → (case species-chiral (con-species c) of
    false → mixture-chiral r
    true → (case con-excess c of true → true; false → mixture-chiral r))
